# ProcMon Recipe: file_io_only
#
# This is a *text descriptor*, not ProcMon's undocumented binary .pmc
# format. The MCP server cannot construct a real .pmc without ProcMon
# itself, so we ship the filter set as text and the operator
# reconstructs it in the ProcMon UI (Filter -> Filter...) or via
# /LoadConfig after generating a binary .pmc once and copying it.
#
# To reconstruct in the ProcMon UI:
# 1. Filter -> Reset Filter (clears defaults).
# 2. Add each Include rule listed below (Filter -> Filter...).
# 3. Add each Exclude rule.
# 4. File -> Save Filter... to persist as a .pmf the GUI understands,
#    or File -> Export Configuration... to save a .pmc the CLI can
#    load with /LoadConfig.
#
# Recipe contract:
# - Capture only File-class events.
# - Suppress noisy event sources: Registry, Network, Process,
#   Profiling.
# - Default Result column unfiltered (operator can add
#   `Result != SUCCESS` post-load if they only want failures).

[Includes]
Operation contains CreateFile
Operation contains ReadFile
Operation contains WriteFile
Operation contains CloseFile
Operation contains QueryDirectory
Operation contains QueryInformationFile
Operation contains SetInformationFile
Operation contains FileSystemControl
Operation contains LockFile
Operation contains UnlockFile

[Excludes]
Operation contains RegQuery
Operation contains RegOpenKey
Operation contains RegCloseKey
Operation contains RegSetValue
Operation contains RegEnumKey
Operation contains TCP
Operation contains UDP
Operation contains Process Create
Operation contains Process Exit
Operation contains Thread Create
Operation contains Thread Exit
Operation contains Process Profiling

[Capture]
BackingFile suggestion: C:\procmon\file_io.pml
Runtime suggestion: 60 seconds
